 "title": "Red eye: red flags decide whether it is vision threatening. Without them it is the lids, a conjunctivitis told apart by its discharge and itch, a subconjunctival hemorrhage or a corneal abrasion; with them it is keratitis, anterior uveitis or acute angle closure glaucoma and needs urgent ophthalmology; each column gives the presentation, the exam finding that decides it and the treatment",
